<!-- ============ CAPABILITY INDEX ============ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;" id="capabilities">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Capability Index</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Capability index: native or connected.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Every capability documented on this site, in one list. <strong>Native</strong> means it ships in the same codebase as the POS. <strong>Connected</strong> means it integrates with a system you choose.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="capx-wrap">
      <table class="capx">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">What it covers</th><th scope="col">Delivery</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Selling &amp; transactions</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Mobile POS</th><td>Full POS on iPhone and iPad, sold from anywhere on the floor rather than a fixed cash wrap.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Payments</th><td>Tap to Pay on iPhone, contactless, chip, swipe, split tender, gift cards, BNPL, foreign-currency cash. Processor-agnostic.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Promotions &amp; loyalty engine</th><td>Thresholds, multi-item BOGO, stackable and customer-specific coupons, tax exemptions, identical across channels.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Line-level control</th><td>Per-line discounts, price overrides, associate attribution, gift messaging, suspend and retrieve, all permissioned and logged.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Returns &amp; exchanges</th><td>Cross-channel returns and exchanges with no sync lag, including promotion-aware bundle returns.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Cash management</th><td>Drawer memos, shared drawers, paid-in/paid-out, blind counts with management sign-off, end-of-day reconciliation and fiscal summaries.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Shopper display</th><td>Second customer-facing screen running targeted content and offers alongside the transaction.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>

          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Inventory &amp; RFID</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Inventory control</th><td>Item-level visibility across stores, warehouses and channels; receiving, transfers and adjustments from the device.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Counting</th><td>Full-store counts in about 20 minutes and targeted cycle counts, without closing the door.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">End-to-end RFID</th><td>Source tagging, EPC commissioning, unit control ledger, RFID checkout and self-checkout, EAS loss prevention, no middleware.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">RFID hardware</th><td>Certified readers, sleds, bins, counter pads and tag printers from Bluebird, Zebra, Impinj, Honeywell and Epson.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>

          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Order management &amp; fulfilment</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Order routing</th><td>Order Fill Logic selects the fulfilment location; split shipments and incoming/outgoing queues.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Omnichannel plays</th><td>BOPIS, curbside, reserve in store, ship-from-store, Endless Aisle, Save the Sale, BORIS.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Carriers &amp; warehouse</th><td>Shipping carriers, warehouse management and returns automation.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>

          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Product &amp; customer data</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Product information (PIM)</th><td>One product record with structured attributes, imagery, translations, catalog imports, brand concepts and seasonal staging.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Customer data (CDP)</th><td>Profiles, marketing consent, QR self sign-up, feedback capture and customer APIs, without a separate CRM migration.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Clienteling</th><td>360-degree profiles at the point of sale, outreach and lookbooks sent by the associate.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">AI at the point of sale</th><td>121 Commerce: product answers, recommendations and next actions drawn from the product and customer records.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Marketing &amp; CRM platforms</th><td>Audience and campaign tools such as Klaviyo and Mailchimp.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>

          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Analytics</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Reporting</th><td>Cloud HQ with 150+ prebuilt retail reports, custom KPIs, segment views and scheduled distribution.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">BI dashboards</th><td>Looker dashboards out of the box; onward BI and data platforms by integration.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>

          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">People &amp; access</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Identity &amp; permissions</th><td>Matrixed rights across hundreds of corporate actions, rotating QR sign-in, every action attributable to a person.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Enterprise identity</th><td>Integrates with the identity provider you already run (Active Directory, SSO and MFA) rather than adding another user store.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Biometric sign-in</th><td>Optional multi-user facial recognition on shared devices, off by default and governed by the retailer.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Device management</th><td>Company-owned and personal devices governed side by side, with policy per device type.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Training &amp; certification</th><td>Role-based assignment from the team member record, course builder and library, certifications, material synced from live product data.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>

          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Global operations</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Fiscal compliance</th><td>Automated compliance across 40+ countries (VAT, GST, NF525, TSE) with locally required fiscal summaries.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Multi-currency &amp; language</th><td>Configured per market from one dashboard, with destination-jurisdiction tax on shipped orders.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Regional payment methods</th><td>QR wallets, digital invoicing in China, installment selection in South Korea, market-specific merchant platforms.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>

          <tr class="capx-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Platform</th></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Hosting</th><td>Google Cloud Platform. AWS, Azure, Tencent and hybrid deployments supported by request.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Offline resilience</th><td>Store-and-Forward keeps every terminal fully operational through an outage, encrypting locally and syncing on reconnect.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Extensibility</th><td>Open APIs for import and export; custom services and logic overlays through external APIs without altering the core.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Interface configuration</th><td>Module sequence, order and exposure set per retailer rather than developed.</td><td><span class="capx-n">Native</span></td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Enterprise systems</th><td>ERP including SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics and NetSuite; marketplaces, accounting, fraud, traffic counters and legacy internal systems.</td><td><span class="capx-c">Connected</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="arch-caption">Every row is documented elsewhere on this site. Anything you need that is not on this list is a question worth putting to a solutions architect rather than assuming either way.</p>
  </div>
</section>

